  "source": "The Anglican Cycle of Prayer",
  "sourceFile": "\"September 2026-December 2026 Anglican Cycle of Prayer.pdf\", provided directly by Josh via Google Drive (file id 1PnFqfTnD3ZEjzU3-ZCinNxRb5LObO1xQ, folder \"TEC Cycle of Prayer\", id 1RNfB4mX7RnVbs9XRHOvO6DhYZ8txZuew).",
  "ingested": "2026-09-29",
  "notes": [
    "This is the single scope-'communion' file: the worldwide Anglican Cycle of Prayer, published by the Anglican Communion Office, rotating daily through the Communion's dioceses and provinces -- the 'Communion' tier of the four-tier Communion/Provincial/Diocesan/Parish Authorized Intercessions structure Josh described. It is not scoped to any one diocese (no `diocese`/`dioceseShort` fields, per schema.json).",
    "Coverage is PARTIAL-YEAR by design, not an error: the source document itself only covers 2026-09-01 through 2026-12-31 (Josh's own Drive file is titled \"September 2026-December 2026 Anglican Cycle of Prayer\"). The January-August 2026 portion of this same annual cycle was not supplied and is not fabricated here, consistent with this corpus's existing partial-year precedent (e.g. episcopal-alabama-2026.json, episcopal-arizona-2026.json).",
    "Each day names either a specific diocese together with the member church/province it belongs to (subject type 'diocese', e.g. 'The Diocese of Belize' / 'The Church in the Province of the West Indies'), or an entire member church/province with no specific diocese singled out (subject type 'province', e.g. 'The Anglican Church of Tanzania' alone) -- this is the source's own distinction, not an inconsistency introduced in transcription. Every Sunday in the source names a province rather than a specific diocese.",
    "The source PDF is a multi-column monthly grid (three columns of dates per page). A linearized copy-pasted text extraction of it silently swapped which diocese/province belonged to which day within the same week (concretely: an initial extraction attributed 'The Anglican Church of Tanzania' to Friday 4 September, when the source's own rendered page layout shows that belongs to Friday 11 September's Diocese of Biharamulo entry, with Friday 4 September actually naming the Diocese of Benin). This file was transcribed only after downloading the actual PDF and reading its rendered page layout, per the corresponding rule added to schema.json's own `rules` array.",
    "Diocese/province names, and the liturgical annotations (Season of Creation, Sunday-after-Trinity labels, etc.) in `liturgicalNote`, are transcribed exactly as printed, including inconsistent internal capitalization/punctuation across entries (e.g. 'The Church of Nigeria (Anglican Communion)' vs. 'Province of the Episcopal Church of South Sudan' vs. 'Eglise Anglicane du Rwanda' with no definite article) and the source's own apparent duplicate-name case ('The Diocese of Christ the King' appears twice, Nov 18 and Nov 19, naming two different provinces -- Mozambique & Angola, then Southern Africa -- preserved as printed rather than treated as an error, since two dioceses sharing a name across different provinces is unremarkable and not this corpus's place to adjudicate).",
    "Not yet wired into any UI or rendering -- this file exists in the corpus but js/cycles-of-prayer.js has no loader/registry concept for scope-'communion' files yet (its current registry and cache-key logic are diocese-centric). Surfacing this as the 'Communion' line in the BCP Authorized Intercessions rubric slot is a separate, not-yet-done step."
  ],
